 `lib/semblr-config.test.ts` | New test cases for `routingEnabled` resolution matrix. |\n| `lib/routing.ts` *(new)* | Pure helpers: `REPORTED_PHASES`, `MVP_PHASE_MODEL_MAP`, `MAX_SWITCHES_PER_CYCLE`, `ABSOLUTE_SWITCH_LIMIT`, `buildSwitchAnnouncement`, `buildPhaseTransitionNote`, `isReportedPhase`, `resolveModelId`. |\n| `lib/routing.test.ts` *(new)* | Data-integrity + formatter tests. |\n| `lib/state.ts` | `RoundState` gains `reportedPhase`, `phaseNote`, `phaseSwitchesThisCycle`. `SessionState` gains `totalPhaseSwitches`, `injectedPhaseTransitionRounds: Set<string>`. |\n| `lib/state.test.ts` | Defaults + reset semantics. |\n| `lib/context-format.ts` | New `buildPhaseTransitionSectionContent(note)` helper. |\n| `lib/context-format.test.ts` | Test the new section builder. |\n| `lib/context-messages.ts` | Extend `assembleContextPrefix` with optional `phaseTransitionMsg`. |\n| `lib/round-data.ts` | *(Optional)* Add `reportedPhase?` + `phaseNote?` to `RoundData` for observability. |\n| `src/semblr.ts` | Register `semblr_report_phase` tool inside `session_start` (per existing pattern, line 1305); add routing block at end of `agent_end`; inject phase-transition note in `context` hook. |\n| `README.md`, `VISION.md` | Short \"Multi-Model Routing (experimental)\" section + roadmap entry. AGENTS.md unchanged. |\n\n## 4. Implementation Phases (ordered, dependencies explicit)\n\n1. **Config layer** — `lib/semblr-config.ts` + test. *No deps.* Unblocks feature gating.\n2. **Pure routing helpers** — `lib/routing.ts` (new) + test. *No deps.* All decision logic, no I/O.\n3. **State layer** — `lib/state.ts` + test. *No deps.* Round/session fields.\n4. **Context layer** — `lib/context-format.ts` + `lib/context-messages.ts` + test. *No deps.* Builds the `[PHASE TRANSITION NOTE]` section.\n5. **Tool registration** — register `semblr_report_phase` in `src/semblr.ts` `session_start`. *Depends on #2 (type guard), #3 (state).* Tool only stores intent.\n6. **Switch logic at `agent_end`** — routing block in `src/semblr.ts`. *Depends on #1, #2, #3, `pi.setModel` API.* Includes the 3 / 5 limits, `ctx.modelRegistry.find()` lookup, `ctx.ui.notify` for success + styled error on failure.\n7. **Note injection at `context`** — uses `buildPhaseTransitionSectionContent` + `assembleContextPrefix` extension + `injectedPhaseTransitionRounds` Set. *Depends on #3, #4.*\n8. **Integration test** — fake `pi` + `ctx` harness simulating `agent_end` with model-registry stub, asserting `setModel` called/not called per matrix (4 switch conditions, limits, idempotency, `null` phase, missing model).\n9. **`npm run verify`** — typecheck, lint, knip, coverage ≥ 80%.\n10. **Docs** — README section + VISION roadmap entry.\n\n## 5. Key Design Decisions\n\n- **Switch only at `agent_end`** — never mid-response. Tool calls during a round overwrite state; only the last report counts, and the switch fires *after* the response.\n- **`null` in map = no switch** — `exploring` stays on user's model. Cheap no-op path: skip silently, do not announce, do not increment counter.\n- **Hardcoded map, no config knobs in MVP** — no presets, no `phaseModels`, no `maxSwitchesPerCycle`, no slash command, no TUI widget. All future tunables explicitly out of scope per comment #1.\n- **Opt-in default** — `routing.enabled: false` (settings) OR `SEMBLR_ROUTING_ENABLED=true` (env). No behavior change when disabled.\n- **Idempotent note injection** — `injectedPhaseTransitionRounds: Set<string>` ensures each note appears exactly once per session.\n- **Last-call-wins for phase report** — multiple tool calls in one round collapse to the final `(phase, note)`.\n- **Pure helpers isolated in `lib/routing.ts`** — keeps the testable surface small; `semblr.ts` becomes a thin wiring layer.\n- **Tool registered inside `session_start`** — matches existing `semblr_checkpoint` pattern (factory-level registration unreliable for LLM visibility).\n\n## 6. Risks & Open Questions\n\n### Risks\n- **LLM may not call the tool** — feature is dead. Mitigation: clear `promptSnippet`; MVP is explicitly a data-gathering experiment.\n- **KV-cache thrash per switch** — cost regression. Mitigation: 3/5 switch limits cap damage; document in README.\n- **Ollama-Cloud models absent from user's `models.json`** — `setModel` fails. Mitigation: opt-in default; surface visible error; pre-check via `ctx.modelRegistry.find()`.\n- **Missing API key for target** — `setModel` returns `false`. Mitigation: spec requires styled error message; stay on current model.\n\n### Open Questions (flag in PR description)\n1. **3 vs 5 limit semantics** — comment #1 step 6 (cap=3, silent bail) vs step 10 (>5 suppresses with warning). Simplest reading: 3 = silent cap, 5 = warn + suppress remainder. **Pick one and call it out.**\n2. **Model id parsing** — `\"glm-5.2:cloud\"` is not standard `provider/id`. Add a `resolveModelId(mapValue, registry)` helper covering: literal match, split on `/` for `provider/id`, or treat `:cloud` as Ollama tag. **No spec pin; implementer has latitude — make it testable.**\n3. **\"Agent cycle\"** — read as `agent_start` → `agent_end` window. Counter resets on `agent_start`.\n4. **First-round note** — if round #1 triggers a switch, no prior note exists → drop silently.\n5. **Mid-compaction tool calls** — out of scope; Semblr cancels compaction anyway.\n6. **Idempotent announcement** — only announce on the first successful switch of a round (spec silent; recommended).\n7. **Save phase/note to round JSON?** — not required; recommended as optional `RoundData` fields for observability/debugging.\n\n## 7. Out of Scope (MVP, per comment #1)\n\nNo presets · no `phaseModels` user config · no tunables (`maxSwitchesPerCycle`, `maxConsecutiveStuck`, `minTurnsPerPhase`, `announceSwitches`, `escalationModel`, `logLevel`) · no `/semblr:routing` slash command · no TUI status-bar widget · no phase indicators.\n---issue 86 brief---\ntotal 8\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 vedat users 4096 Jun 24 08:29 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 vedat users 4096 Jun 24 08:42 ..\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1782290909451}}
